{"abstract":"Digital methods, taken up in the collection and analysis of data, raise concerns around extraction, representation, care, consent, and participation familiar to feminist methodologies. At a feminist STS lab, specialising in digital methods, we convened some workshops to support research design in ongoing projects situated in the Lab’s community, with the aim to articulate feminist principles for digital methods. These projects, working with methods including digital ethnography, database implementation, and machine learning design raise feminist questions around centring care in data collection and participation, navigating hesitancies around extracting data from vulnerable subjects, and working through representational politics of data. These workshops, rather than congealing a set of feminist principles, generated a proliferation of disconcertments and troubles. We offer workshopping troubles as a way to navigate and theorise tensions in designing digital methods research. We account for how these workshops served as a method to elicit troubles, surfacing them for further analysis, and helped us shift from binding dichotomies to troubles that open ongoing inquiry. We reflect on how digital methods return us to troubles that, while well understood in feminist approaches to data, require articulation in practice and research design.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Perriam, Jessamy","Cohn, Marisa","Hockenhull, Michael","Tatjana Reime, Lara","Landa, Luis","Kjær, Katrine Meldgaard","Friis, Henriette"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730171"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Disconcertment","Ethnography","Feminist digital methods","Research Design","Science and Technology Studies","workshopping"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"workshopping troubles towards feminist digital methods","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/08164649.2024.2321576","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730171","identifier":[{"id":"85186618045","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-63137823-9862-4f33-a0d3-440a4269c108"],"keyword":["Feminist digital methods","disconcertment","ethnography","research design","science and technology studies","workshopping"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-70A0FC14E3B5B57117B14FBB1F3E6C98"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/08164649.2024.2321576","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Digital Welfare","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jessamy","key":"perriampau","last":"Perriam","locid":"4ca57c3b-1d1f-4ecf-87b0-fe690510c887","name":"Perriam, Jessamy","orcid":"0000-0002-6362-8634","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"hockenhullpau","last":"Hockenhull","locid":"5041f387-908f-4845-9f79-3a6dbd527f4b","name":"Hockenhull, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-2670-2102","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lara","key":"reimepau","last":"Reime","locid":"0baaf9f8-3126-4cb1-b22f-b9fceabb8b54","name":"Tatjana Reime, Lara","name_org":"Reime, Lara","orcid":"0000-0002-7475-2147","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Luis","key":"landapau","last":"Landa","name":"Landa, Luis","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Meldgaard","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"0c46864b-a7f8-4439-aeda-0781f77bfe88","name":"Kjær, Katrine Meldgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7994-5186","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henriette","key":"friispau","last":"Friis","locid":"140f881b-1540-455b-8066-f0bc9ac6d82c","name":"Friis, Henriette","orcid":"0009-0008-1098-6674","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-63137823-9862-4f33-a0d3-440a4269c108"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Workshopping Troubles: Towards Feminist Digital Methods","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730171","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we offer a collective, multi-vocal reflection on using poetry for research purposes. These were reflections on an online sub-plenary session organized as a workshop, which was held at the European Group for Organization Studies conference in 2021. During this workshop, the first three authors presented a step-by-step method for doing poetic inquiry and invited participants to apply it to their own empirical data or research praxis. The method was created in response to the marginalization of affect and embodiment in mainstream research in organization studies. Poetic inquiry aims to formulate specific practices of “writing differently” that assist researchers in their attempts to analyze and articulate their findings in embodied and affective ways. In this paper, we describe the method and bring together multi-vocal reflections from the participants and organizers of the workshop on the affects of poetic inquiry and the (ethical) questions that it poses.","author_count":12,"contributors":["van Amsterdam, Noortje","van Eck, Dide","Kjær, Katrine Meldgaard","Brown, Anna","de Coster, Marjan","Lafaire, Ana Paula","Leclair, Margot","Pullen, Allison","Theunissen, Anne","Thomson, Alistair","Tremblay, Maryse","Quental, Camilla"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730184"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","Belgium","Canada","Finland","France","Netherlands","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Aalto University","Aix-Marseille University","All Global Affiliations","Audencia School of Management and Communication","Hasselt University","KU Leuven","Macquarie University","University of Quebec Montreal","University of St Andrews","University of Tasmania","Utrecht University"],"keyword":["Affect","Embodiment","Feminist praxis","Poetic inquiry","Writing differently"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feeling clumsy and curious a collective reflection on using poetry as an unconventional method at a conventional conference","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/gwao.12964","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730184","identifier":[{"id":"85148626026","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a10f30c4-479e-48a8-84e7-62881270a1d6"],"keyword":["Affect","Embodiment","Feminist praxis","Poetic inquiry","Writing differently"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3E5394030EE92E39A9606CF47218C3B6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://research-repository.st-andrews.ac.uk/bitstream/handle/10023/27021/van_Amsterdam_2023_GWO_Feeling_clumsy_CC.pdf?sequence=1&isAllowed=y","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/epdf/10.1111/gwao.12964","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/gwao.12964","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"utrecht university","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Utrecht University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"be","key":"ku leuven","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"KU Leuven","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technolo