":"On the Intracist and Speaking in Tongues","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381586","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In this article, we suggest approaching writing as a vulnerable practice marked by an unstable boundary between bodies: bodies of text and bodies of writers. We present an exercise-method that we refer to as Monster Writing, which we have developed in order to engage with these instabilities as well as in order to address experiences of difficulty, anxiety and uncertainty in relation with the text and writing process. Though the writing process can at times be exciting and thrilling, and at other times perhaps a little tedious and mundane, for some it also presents (more than) occasional encounters with one's own insecurities, shame and doubt. We argue that this potentially more painful relationship between writer and text should be awarded more attention in scholarship on writing, and that a way of doing so is through the framework of feminist theory on vulnerability, embodiment, and the monstrous.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Henriksen, Line","Kjær, Katrine Meldgaard","Blønd, Marie","Cohn, Marisa","Cakici, Baki","Douglas-Jones, Rachel","Ferreira, Pedro","Feshak, Viktoriya","Gahoonia, Simy Kaur","Sandbukt, Sunniva"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383081"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Technical University of Munich"],"keyword":["Feminist theory","Monster theory","Organizational studies","Vulnerability","Writing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"writing bodies and bodies of text thinking vulnerability through monsters","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/gwao.12782","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383081","identifier":[{"id":"85121653378","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7b7818dc-cf90-442f-826c-fe4264251f64"],"keyword":["feminist theory","monster theory","organizational studies","vulnerability","writing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5993E6636350380725B0F7E6033835DC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/gwao.12782","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/gwao.12782","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"technical university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Munich","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","name":"Henriksen, Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Meldgaard","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"0c46864b-a7f8-4439-aeda-0781f77bfe88","name":"Kjær, Katrine Meldgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7994-5186","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"bløndpau","last":"Blønd","name":"Blønd, Marie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marisa","key":"cohnpau","last":"Cohn","locid":"e9d14210-bc71-4824-b7cf-fd1448d022ab","name":"Cohn, Marisa","orcid":"0000-0002-3912-2166","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Baki","key":"cakicipau","last":"Cakici","locid":"b614ac6f-eefa-44a3-8b9a-092b88d86d37","name":"Cakici, Baki","orcid":"0000-0002-1039-8177","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rachel","key":"douglasjonespau","last":"Douglas-Jones","locid":"f11b0cc1-ad9f-4b12-b805-65b70e5bcd65","name":"Douglas-Jones, Rachel","orcid":"0000-0001-9562-6572","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pedro","key":"ferreirapau","last":"Ferreira","locid":"1b3cff7f-1549-4998-b52e-0ba9093e1d01","name":"Ferreira, Pedro","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Viktoriya","key":"feshakpau","last":"Feshak","name":"Feshak, Viktoriya","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Simy Kaur","key":"gahooniapau","last":"Gahoonia","locid":"6c543b1d-8137-489d-b444-d17921fc9de9","name":"Gahoonia, Simy Kaur","orcid":"0000-0001-9668-6868","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sunniva","key":"sandbuktpau","last":"Sandbukt","locid":"06d038a4-f659-4c53-8a6d-58e295ab603f","name":"Sandbukt, Sunniva","orcid":"0009-0002-4274-4991","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/gwao.12782","issn":["09686673","14680432"],"issn_org":["09686673"],"journal":"Gender, Work and Organization","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Gender, Work and Organization"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121653378"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7b7818dc-cf90-442f-826c-fe4264251f64"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Writing bodies and bodies of text: Thinking vulnerability through monsters","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383081","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This paper considers the ways in which silences and absences are a central part of research that relies on automated data collection from social media or the internet. In recent years, automated data collection driven or supported research methods have gained popularity within the social sciences and humanities. With this increase in popularity, it becomes ever more pertinent to consider how to engage with digital data, and how both engagement and data are situated, messy, and contingent. Based on experiences with “missing” data, this paper mobilizes the framework of hauntology to make sense of what relationships may be built with missing data and how silences haunt research practices. Ultimately, we argue that it is possible to reimagine absent data not as a limitation but as an invitation to reflect on and establish new methods for working with automated data collections.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kjær, Katrine Meldgaard","Ojala, Mace","Henriksen, Line"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382247"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Absence","Data","Ghosts","Hauntology","Twitter"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"absent data engagements with absence in a twitter collection","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.28968/cftt.v7i2.34563","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382247","ids":["itu-421b9e27-2e97-4f3e-b59e-120bf2cf9fe9"],"keyword":["Twitter","absence","data","ghosts","hauntology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-D7D5392DAE4CBE5BE270F9172ED4065A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.28968/cftt.v7i2.34563","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://catalystjournal.org/index.php/catalyst/article/view/34563/28500","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Meldgaard","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"0c46864b-a7f8-4439-aeda-0781f77bfe88","name":"Kjær, Katrine Meldgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7994-5186","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mace","key":"ojalapau","last":"Ojala","name":"Ojala, Mace","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","name":"Henriksen, Line","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.28968/cftt.v7i2.34563","issn":["23803312"],"issue":"2","journal":"Catalyst: Feminism, Theory, Technoscience","pages":"1-21","status":"p","title":"Catalyst: Feminism, Theory, Technoscience","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-421b9e27-2e97-4f3e-b59e-120bf2cf9fe9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Absent Data : Engagements with absence in a Twitter collection","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382247","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
