arsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The author considers the relationship between bodies, food, and the construction of the “obese” subject in Oprah Winfrey’s self-help book Make the Connection and Morgan Spurlock’s film Super Size Me. Interestingly, the process of becoming “obese” in these texts has very little to do with gaining weight. Instead, it is highly dependent on Winfrey and Spurlock’s relationship to food and eating, and the circumstances in which this eating takes place. Accordingly, the article argues that to truly understand how subjects are created as a part of the “obesity epidemic” here, one must examine the relationship between bodies and the objects they interact with.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Kjær, Katrine Meldgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-579308"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Eating","Food","Intra activity","obesity epidemic"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"food body intra activity and the relational obese subject in super size me and make the connection","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84994666662","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-579308","identifier":[{"id":"84994666662","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-1557c849-def2-4c9a-8493-7129d2702a7b"],"keyword":["Eating","Oprah Winfrey","Super Size Me","food","intra-activity","“obesity epidemic”"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B8E809D92404A1C3BEE7702B9EE8E200"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department for the Study of Culture","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Language, Cultural Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Meldgaard","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"de12158d-82f2-461a-af08-b9227d1cefef","name":"Kjær, Katrine Meldgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7994-5186","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/21604851.2017.1242293","issn":["21604851","2160486X"],"issn_org":["21604851"],"issue":"1","journal":"Fat Studies","pages":"77-89","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Fat Studies","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84994666662"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-1557c849-def2-4c9a-8493-7129d2702a7b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Food-Body Intra-Activity and the Relational “Obese” Subject in Super Size Me and Make the Connection","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-579308","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
